{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "description": "The state machine that decides whether the application may run. Pure: a cached snapshot plus a clock in, one state out. Both editions must agree on every case, because a disagreement means one platform locks a paying customer out while the other lets a revoked licence keep running.",
  "notes": [
    "Times are ISO 8601 with an offset. The evaluator works in UTC.",
    "'now' is what the machine's clock says. 'clockHighWater' is the latest time this installation has ever seen, kept inside the encrypted cache.",
    "A snapshot of null means there is no cache at all."
  ],
  "cases": [
